jewbuntu-skin (0.1.0~git20261112.2+26.04) resolute; urgency=medium

  * GTK4 theme built in libadwaita mode (MacTahoe's --libadwaita colour handling,
    for the installed theme): it uses libadwaita's colour variables and draws
    borders from currentColor. Apps that colour their own windows (Terminal,
    Ptyxis) now get readable menus and title bars: before, menu items kept the
    skin's dark text on Terminal's dark menus, and title-bar buttons and the
    title-bar edge stayed white. GTK3 styles are unchanged.

 -- Jewbuntu Developers <maintainers@jewbuntu.invalid>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:21:16 -0500

jewbuntu-skin (0.1.0~git20261112.1+26.04) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Build without MacTahoe's --blur option. That variant makes app windows 75%
    opaque, expecting Blur my Shell to blur what is behind them; Jewbuntu keeps
    application blur off (it boxed the dock), so windows were see-through with
    no blur. Windows are now 96% opaque, as on macOS; the dock, top bar and
    menus keep their glass (GNOME Shell styles are not affected by --blur).

 -- Jewbuntu Developers <maintainers@jewbuntu.invalid>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:15:47 -0500

